.TH byobu-enable-agent-hooks 1 "18 November 2026" byobu "byobu"
.SH NAME
byobu-enable-agent-hooks, byobu-disable-agent-hooks \- have Claude Code report what it is doing to byobu

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbyobu-enable-agent-hooks\fP
.TP
\fBbyobu-disable-agent-hooks\fP

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBbyobu-enable-agent-hooks\fP adds a hook for each Claude Code event that changes what it is doing (a prompt submitted, a tool run, a permission asked for, a turn finished or failed, the session started or ended) to Claude Code's user settings, \fI~/.claude/settings.json\fP (or \fI$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/settings.json\fP). Each runs \fBbyobu-agent-state \-\-claude-hook\fP, which records the state on the tmux pane Claude Code runs in: byobu's window list then marks each window by what its agent is doing: \fB?\fP blocked waiting for you, \fB\[u2717]\fP failed, \fB\[u25C9]\fP done, \fB\[u25D4]\fP working. See \fBbyobu-agent-state\fP(1).

Everything else in the settings file is kept; the previous file is saved as \fIsettings.json.byobu-backup\fP. Running it again leaves one set of hooks. The hooks take effect in Claude Code sessions started afterwards, and do nothing outside tmux (3.2 or later).

\fBbyobu-disable-agent-hooks\fP removes those hooks, and nothing else.

.SH SEE ALSO
.PD 0
